Results.ReviewText:
I have shopped for a while for a grill that is well built, cooks even, and I don't need a loan to buy.   After much research, this is the one I went with.  For context, I normally cook for 5-8 people, and I am grilling 2-3 times a week year around.  I have had this for about a month.

The Great:  Weber Customer Service - i had a problem, they made it right immediately

The good:  grill even-ness front to back and side to side is wonderful;  overall sturdy & well made; easy to put together;  really like the gas gauge;  it has really improved my cooking game; I like the fold down side;  access to grease tray from front;  thermometer on lid is accurate;

A little below expectations: temperature consistency on long low grills had almost a 30 deg variation;  the low setting is more of a medium, so with one burner on low, i can't get below 200 deg;  the spot for the iGrill is not magnetic, making it useless;  wish both sides folded down;  

Overall:   The best grill I have used in this price range, although i wish it was a little bigger
